  "q1_wrong": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "consul.Server", "note": "Several retained_via_interfaces rows were runtime false positives that I had to verify by reading wiring: OverviewManager and usagemetrics 'StateProvider' rows actually hold s.fsm not the server; serverdiscovery.Config 'EventPublisher' and connectca 'EventPublisher' rows hold s.publisher; submatview.LocalMaterializerDeps 'LocalBackend' holds an EventPublisher in proxycfg-glue but the PeeringBackend in peerstream — the tool itself flagged this as unverified"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server (callers)", "note": "called_by edges listed aclTokenReplicator/aclPolicyReplicator/aclRoleReplicator, which turned out to receive srv *Server as a call argument (acl_replication.go:47-91), not retain it — correct as call edges but I had to read to exclude them from the retention audit"}
  ],
  "q2_fallbacks": [
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "consul.Server", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "Function-value retention (closures stored in struct fields). The index_caveat itself admitted this gap; grep on 'GetStore:' / 'server.FSM()' found ~12 closure holders Sense never surfaced: acl gRPC Config funcs (acl/server.go:23-30), servercert.CertManager (agent.go:719), proxycfgglue ServerDataSourceDeps + 20 retaining structs (agent.go:4659), catalogproxycfg.ConfigSource (agent.go:955), xdscapacity (server.go:828), usagemetrics GetMembersFunc, CertExpirationMonitor.Query, FunctionReplicator.ReplicateFn"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query": "consul.Server", "fallback": "read", "missing": "Runtime satisfier of each interface row — the retained_note said 'which satisfier the field holds at runtime is unverified', so I read server_grpc.go:37-543, server.go:560-890, agent.go wiring to confirm or reject every one of the 31 rows"},
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query": "consul.Server (composed_by)", "fallback": "grep", "missing": "Completeness assurance for the audit — I ran 'grep -rn \"srv *\\*Server\"' over agent/consul as the mandated spot-check; it confirmed the composed_by list but also surfaced CertExpirationMonitor's field at leader_metrics.go:127 vs Sense's struct ref :114, i.e. field-level line precision"}
  ],
  "q3_hints": [
    {"tool": "sense_graph", "query_before": "consul.Server (callers)", "query_after": "sense_blast consul.Server", "hint": "next_steps said: '54 callers reach this - run sense_blast for full change impact and what holds it (retained_via_interfaces, holders that keep it behind an interface and never name it)' — I ran blast in the same batch and retained_via_interfaces became the core of Step 4"},
    {"tool": "sense_blast", "query_before": "trusting retained_via_interfaces rows as holders", "query_after": "grep sweep for GetStore:/closure captures", "hint": "index_caveat text 'Static graph may miss: method-on-field dispatch, function-value passing (handlers stored as fields)' directly prompted the closure-capture grep sweep that found the highest-risk holder class of the whole audit"}
  ],
  "q4_value": "The retained_via_interfaces table from one sense_blast call: a precomputed list of 31 holder→interface→carrier→Server chains (e.g. rate.Handler via ServersStatusProvider via serverACLResolverBackend) spanning packages that never import agent/consul — recovering that with grep would have required knowing each local interface name in advance.",
  "q5_improve": "Extend retention analysis to stored function values: a closure assigned to a struct field (GetStore/ForwardRPC) that captures the target symbol is exactly the same lifecycle hazard as an interface-typed field, and this session it was the entire top-risk class that Sense only acknowledged in a caveat string.",
  "score": 9,
  "score_rationale": "Q1's retained_via_interfaces chains (cross-package interface retention like rate/handler.go:164 and internal/storage/raft/backend.go:80) are things grep could not have enumerated without already knowing every local interface name, placing this in the 9-10 band; the closure-holder gap and unverified runtime satisfiers (Q2) that forced grep/read fallbacks keep it at 9 rather than 10."
}
